[[:db/retract 17592186152491 :question/answer-fields 17592186149518] [:db/retract 17592186152492 :question/answer-fields 17592186149519] [:db/retract 17592186152498 :question/answer-fields 17592186149547] [:db/retract 17592186152498 :question/answer-fields 17592186149550] {:db/id 17592186152062 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-06e3421b-201f-5b72-a27d-eae8c015169e" "question-1c49d9f9-921f-55ef-bb6f-a2909dfca013" "question-60b1fda4-60e8-5732-9f6d-dacad47edd54" "question-0c1ec073-8757-564a-9c57-9cebe1d4c92b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186151865 :question/problem "Is the following statement true or false?\n\nThe integer $21$ is the additive inverse of $14$ modulo $35.$" :question/worked-solution "The additive inverse of $14$ modulo $35$ is the integer $0 \\leq x \\lt 35$ such that\n\n$$\nx + 14 \\equiv 0 \\quad (\\textrm{mod}\\:35).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that when we add our two numbers, we get a number that is congruent to zero modulo $35{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}21+14 & ≡35 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,35) \\\\  & ≡0 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,35)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the statement is true." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152063 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3323609a-bf83-5586-b0db-68ed80775b56" "question-c6e15ebf-3068-5417-a3c8-7e4572a15b66" "question-0244a7b0-af5a-5462-8463-f5b7c25a67e5" "question-f130e5d0-ce45-5587-8424-e7b9465649e8" "question-57513638-55f0-5e26-b8a8-dbc4daee54c1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186151866 :question/problem "Find the additive inverse of $17$ modulo $26.$" :question/worked-solution "The additive inverse of $17$ modulo $26$ is the integer $0 \\leq x \\lt 26$ such that\n\n$$\nx + 17 \\equiv 0 \\quad (\\textrm{mod}\\:26).\n$$\n\nNotice that $-17 + 17 \\equiv 0,$ so $x\\equiv -17\\:(\\textrm{mod}\\:26).$ To write this in the required form, we use the following sequence of congruences:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ≡-17 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,26) \\\\  & ≡0-17 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,26) \\\\  & ≡26-17 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,26) \\\\  & ≡9 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,26)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $17$ modulo $26$ is $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}9}.$\n\nWe can verify this result as follows:\n\n$$\n9 + 17 \\equiv 26 \\equiv 0\\:\\:{\\color{green}{\\checkmark}} \\quad (\\textrm{mod}\\:26)\n$$\n\n**Note:** The additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a \\: \\textrm{mod} \\: n.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152064 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9e204021-2fb2-5d43-b1c6-38cf42c71b93" "question-03d7746d-d7c7-51a7-a5bf-9cade8e1e535" "question-6be34eb0-fa03-58ac-aac3-09af6a99143a" "question-71d1db00-def0-5962-9ebf-e72a766990a9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186151867 :question/problem "Find the additive inverse of $23$ modulo $15.$" :question/worked-solution "The additive inverse of $23$ modulo $15$ is the integer $0 \\leq x \\lt 15$ such that\n\n$$\nx + 23 \\equiv 0 \\quad (\\textrm{mod}\\:15).\n$$\n\nFirst, we note that $23\\equiv 8\\:(\\textrm{mod}\\:15){:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}23 & ≡1\\cdot 15+8 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,15) \\\\  & ≡1\\cdot 0+8 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,15) \\\\  & ≡8 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,15)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, note that $-8 + 8 \\equiv 0,$ so $x\\equiv -8\\:(\\textrm{mod}\\:15).$ To write this in the required form, we use the following sequence of congruences:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ≡-8 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,15) \\\\  & ≡0-8 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,15) \\\\  & ≡15-8 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,15) \\\\  & ≡7 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,15)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $23$ modulo $15$ is $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}7}.$\n\nWe can verify this result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}23+7≡30≡2\\cdot 15≡0\\,\\,✓\\,(\\text{mod}\\,15)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** In general, the additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a \\: \\textrm{mod} \\: n.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152065 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-087515b4-1dee-5eec-87da-466a8e426d85" "question-0724cde5-d299-58a6-b45c-db140b3f5272" "question-6564674d-f4f6-54d7-8b5f-5cfc473b8c8e" "question-c9d728b0-5a87-57b1-8b30-46d4db7caf62"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186151868 :question/problem "Find the additive inverse of $-43$ modulo $15.$" :question/worked-solution "The additive inverse of $-43$ modulo $15$ is the integer $0 \\leq x \\lt 15$ such that\n\n$$\nx + (-43) \\equiv 0 \\quad (\\textrm{mod}\\:15).\n$$\n\nFirst, we note that $-43\\equiv 2\\:(\\textrm{mod}\\:15){:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-43 & ≡(-3)\\cdot 15+2 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,15) \\\\  & ≡(-3)\\cdot 0+2 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,15) \\\\  & ≡2 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,15)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, note that $-2 + 2 \\equiv 0,$ so $x\\equiv -2\\:(\\textrm{mod}\\:15).$ To write this in the required form, we use the following sequence of congruences:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ≡-2 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,15) \\\\  & ≡0-2 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,15) \\\\  & ≡15-2 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,15) \\\\  & ≡13 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,15)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $-43$ modulo $15$ is $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}13}.$\n\nWe can verify this result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-43+13≡-30≡(-2)\\cdot 15≡0\\,\\,✓\\,(\\text{mod}\\,15)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** In general, the additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a \\: \\textrm{mod} \\: n.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-3323609a-bf83-5586-b0db-68ed80775b56" :question/id #uuid "3323609a-bf83-5586-b0db-68ed80775b56" :question/math-academy-id "q-213391" :question/problem "Expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $42,$ the additive inverse of $29$ modulo $42$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The additive inverse of $29$ modulo $42$ is the integer $0\\le x<42$ such that\n\n$$\nx+29≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,42).\n$$\n\nNotice that $-29+29≡0,$ so $x≡-29\\,(\\text{mod}\\,32).$ To write this in the required form, we use the following sequence of congruences:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ≡-29 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,42) \\\\  & ≡0-29 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,42) \\\\  & ≡42-29 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,42) \\\\  & ≡13 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,42)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $19$ modulo $42$ is $13.$\n\nWe can verify this result as follows:\n\n$$\n13+29≡42≡0\\,\\,✓\\,(\\text{mod}\\,42)\n$$\n\n**Note:** The additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a\\,\\text{mod}\\,n.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b91b14cb-9165-5a96-9804-4f9358ea91de"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b91b14cb-9165-5a96-9804-4f9358ea91de" :answer-field/id #uuid "b91b14cb-9165-5a96-9804-4f9358ea91de" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-7377ff68-7ffb-5b26-80bb-0cac6b01660a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7377ff68-7ffb-5b26-80bb-0cac6b01660a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7377ff68-7ffb-5b26-80bb-0cac6b01660a" :answer/id #uuid "7377ff68-7ffb-5b26-80bb-0cac6b01660a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c6e15ebf-3068-5417-a3c8-7e4572a15b66" :question/id #uuid "c6e15ebf-3068-5417-a3c8-7e4572a15b66" :question/math-academy-id "q-213389" :question/problem "Expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $28,$ the additive inverse of $7$ modulo $28$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The additive inverse of $7$ modulo $28$ is the integer $0\\le x<28$ such that\n\n$$\nx+7≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,28).\n$$\n\nNotice that $-7+7≡0,$ so $x≡-7\\,(\\text{mod}\\,28).$ To write this in the required form, we use the following sequence of congruences:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ≡-7 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,28) \\\\  & ≡0-7 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,28) \\\\  & ≡28-7 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,28) \\\\  & ≡21 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,28)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $7$ modulo $28$ is $21.$\n\nWe can verify this result as follows:\n\n$$\n7+21≡28≡0\\,\\,✓\\,(\\text{mod}\\,28)\n$$\n\n**Note:** The additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a\\,\\text{mod}\\,n.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6540c7d1-2d61-5169-b54f-0d88a3213169"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6540c7d1-2d61-5169-b54f-0d88a3213169" :answer-field/id #uuid "6540c7d1-2d61-5169-b54f-0d88a3213169" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-0b1b9b33-ec22-5e04-89e8-0714d1ed63d8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0b1b9b33-ec22-5e04-89e8-0714d1ed63d8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b1b9b33-ec22-5e04-89e8-0714d1ed63d8" :answer/id #uuid "0b1b9b33-ec22-5e04-89e8-0714d1ed63d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0244a7b0-af5a-5462-8463-f5b7c25a67e5" :question/id #uuid "0244a7b0-af5a-5462-8463-f5b7c25a67e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-213385" :question/problem "Expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $35,$ the additive inverse of $23$ modulo $35$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The additive inverse of $23$ modulo $35$ is the integer $0\\le x<35$ such that\n\n$$\nx+23≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,35).\n$$\n\nNotice that $-23+23≡0,$ so $x≡-23\\,(\\text{mod}\\,35).$ To write this in the required form, we use the following sequence of congruences:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ≡-23 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,35) \\\\  & ≡0-23 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,35) \\\\  & ≡35-23 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,35) \\\\  & ≡12 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,35)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $23$ modulo $35$ is $12.$\n\nWe can verify this result as follows:\n\n$$\n12+23≡35≡0\\,\\,✓\\,(\\text{mod}\\,35)\n$$\n\n**Note:** The additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a\\,\\text{mod}\\,n.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5a868ffa-8556-55e4-8793-d0396f7fabcf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5a868ffa-8556-55e4-8793-d0396f7fabcf" :answer-field/id #uuid "5a868ffa-8556-55e4-8793-d0396f7fabcf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-30bf074a-227f-5233-8f62-fd5916eafb8a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-30bf074a-227f-5233-8f62-fd5916eafb8a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-30bf074a-227f-5233-8f62-fd5916eafb8a" :answer/id #uuid "30bf074a-227f-5233-8f62-fd5916eafb8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f130e5d0-ce45-5587-8424-e7b9465649e8" :question/id #uuid "f130e5d0-ce45-5587-8424-e7b9465649e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-213387" :question/problem "Expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $38,$ the additive inverse of $16$ modulo $38$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The additive inverse of $16$ modulo $38$ is the integer $0\\le x<38$ such that\n\n$$\nx+16≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,38).\n$$\n\nNotice that $-16+16≡0,$ so $x≡-16\\,(\\text{mod}\\,38).$ To write this in the required form, we use the following sequence of congruences:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ≡-16 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,38) \\\\  & ≡0-16 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,38) \\\\  & ≡38-16 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,38) \\\\  & ≡22 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,38)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $16$ modulo $38$ is $22.$\n\nWe can verify this result as follows:\n\n$$\n22+16≡38≡0\\,\\,✓\\,(\\text{mod}\\,38)\n$$\n\n**Note:** The additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a\\,\\text{mod}\\,n.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-68d35404-e6f8-572a-b2b7-4d6b7ef7fcee"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-68d35404-e6f8-572a-b2b7-4d6b7ef7fcee" :answer-field/id #uuid "68d35404-e6f8-572a-b2b7-4d6b7ef7fcee" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-1c299029-b576-5db7-9997-1ad37134903d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1c299029-b576-5db7-9997-1ad37134903d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c299029-b576-5db7-9997-1ad37134903d" :answer/id #uuid "1c299029-b576-5db7-9997-1ad37134903d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "22" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-57513638-55f0-5e26-b8a8-dbc4daee54c1" :question/id #uuid "57513638-55f0-5e26-b8a8-dbc4daee54c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-213382" :question/problem "Expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $22,$ the additive inverse of $14$ modulo $22$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The additive inverse of $14$ modulo $22$ is the integer $0\\le x<22$ such that\n\n$$\nx+14≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,22).\n$$\n\nNotice that $-14+14≡0,$ so $x≡-14\\,(\\text{mod}\\,22).$ To write this in the required form, we use the following sequence of congruences:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ≡-14 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,22) \\\\  & ≡0-14 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,22) \\\\  & ≡22-14 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,22) \\\\  & ≡8 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,22)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $14$ modulo $22$ is $8.$\n\nWe can verify this result as follows:\n\n$$\n8+14≡22≡0\\,\\,✓\\,(\\text{mod}\\,22)\n$$\n\n**Note:** The additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a\\,\\text{mod}\\,n.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-535f82cf-e072-52a9-bc9d-96b1ca0648ea"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-535f82cf-e072-52a9-bc9d-96b1ca0648ea" :answer-field/id #uuid "535f82cf-e072-52a9-bc9d-96b1ca0648ea" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-bcf0d6e5-0050-5d32-96ef-b82f6090aca6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bcf0d6e5-0050-5d32-96ef-b82f6090aca6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bcf0d6e5-0050-5d32-96ef-b82f6090aca6" :answer/id #uuid "bcf0d6e5-0050-5d32-96ef-b82f6090aca6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9e204021-2fb2-5d43-b1c6-38cf42c71b93" :question/id #uuid "9e204021-2fb2-5d43-b1c6-38cf42c71b93" :question/math-academy-id "q-213336" :question/problem "Expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $17,$ the additive inverse of $34$ modulo $17$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The additive inverse of $34$ modulo $17$ is the integer $0\\le x<17$ such that\n\n$$\nx+34≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,17).\n$$\n\nFirst, note that $34≡2\\cdot 17≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,17),$ and $0+0≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,17).$\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $34$ modulo $17$ is $0.$\n\nWe can verify this result as follows:\n\n$$\n34+0≡2\\cdot 17+0≡2\\cdot 0+0≡0\\,\\,✓\\,(\\text{mod}\\,17)\n$$\n\n**Note:** In general, the additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a\\,\\text{mod}\\,n.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1e561b0b-c7fb-5747-abe8-d7ea779b0e25"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1e561b0b-c7fb-5747-abe8-d7ea779b0e25" :answer-field/id #uuid "1e561b0b-c7fb-5747-abe8-d7ea779b0e25" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-9cab45c4-7a25-50f7-a9f8-9b1a3f5031b0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9cab45c4-7a25-50f7-a9f8-9b1a3f5031b0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9cab45c4-7a25-50f7-a9f8-9b1a3f5031b0" :answer/id #uuid "9cab45c4-7a25-50f7-a9f8-9b1a3f5031b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-03d7746d-d7c7-51a7-a5bf-9cade8e1e535" :question/id #uuid "03d7746d-d7c7-51a7-a5bf-9cade8e1e535" :question/math-academy-id "q-213345" :question/problem "Expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $8,$ the additive inverse of $19$ modulo $8$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The additive inverse of $19$ modulo $8$ is the integer $0\\le x<8$ such that\n\n$$\nx+19≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8).\n$$\n\nFirst, we note that $19≡3\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}19 & ≡2\\cdot 8+3 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡2\\cdot 0+3 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡3 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, note that $-3+3≡0,$ so $x≡-3\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8).$ To write this in the required form, we use the following sequence of congruences:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ≡-3 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡0-3 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡8-3 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡5 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $19$ modulo $8$ is $5.$\n\nWe can verify this result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}19+5≡24≡3\\cdot 8≡0\\,\\,✓\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** In general, the additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a\\,\\text{mod}\\,n.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-74b412ab-e118-5b08-8e02-e1a6b6b3e96f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-74b412ab-e118-5b08-8e02-e1a6b6b3e96f" :answer-field/id #uuid "74b412ab-e118-5b08-8e02-e1a6b6b3e96f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e8198a59-dcc6-5fda-9c23-786c260cdb0c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e8198a59-dcc6-5fda-9c23-786c260cdb0c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8198a59-dcc6-5fda-9c23-786c260cdb0c" :answer/id #uuid "e8198a59-dcc6-5fda-9c23-786c260cdb0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id