erse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a\\,\\text{mod}\\,n.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1b63bca3-54e7-56c6-bed9-1bfe3820316e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1b63bca3-54e7-56c6-bed9-1bfe3820316e" :answer-field/id #uuid "1b63bca3-54e7-56c6-bed9-1bfe3820316e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-aa214343-d046-582c-82b3-c94cfea94052" :answer-field/choices ["answer-aa214343-d046-582c-82b3-c94cfea94052"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa214343-d046-582c-82b3-c94cfea94052" :answer/id #uuid "aa214343-d046-582c-82b3-c94cfea94052" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6564674d-f4f6-54d7-8b5f-5cfc473b8c8e" :question/id #uuid "6564674d-f4f6-54d7-8b5f-5cfc473b8c8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-213355" :question/problem "Expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $8,$ the additive inverse of $-30$ modulo $8$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The additive inverse of $-30$ modulo $8$ is the integer $0\\le x<8$ such that\n\n$$\nx+(-30)≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8).\n$$\n\nFirst, we note that $-30≡2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-30 & ≡(-4)\\cdot 8+2 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡(-4)\\cdot 0+2 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡2 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, note that $-2+2≡0,$ so $x≡-2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8).$ To write this in the required form, we use the following sequence of congruences:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ≡-2 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡0-2 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡8-2 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡6 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $-30$ modulo $8$ is $6.$\n\nWe can verify this result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-30+6≡-24≡(-3)\\cdot 8≡0\\,\\,✓\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** In general, the additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a\\,\\text{mod}\\,n.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c8dc1520-5543-5aaa-80d6-e9957a8c2135"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c8dc1520-5543-5aaa-80d6-e9957a8c2135" :answer-field/id #uuid "c8dc1520-5543-5aaa-80d6-e9957a8c2135" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-6bc640fb-3a5b-558b-8451-0fb89a109109" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6bc640fb-3a5b-558b-8451-0fb89a109109"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6bc640fb-3a5b-558b-8451-0fb89a109109" :answer/id #uuid "6bc640fb-3a5b-558b-8451-0fb89a109109" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c9d728b0-5a87-57b1-8b30-46d4db7caf62" :question/id #uuid "c9d728b0-5a87-57b1-8b30-46d4db7caf62" :question/math-academy-id "q-213354" :question/problem "Expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $23,$ the additive inverse of $-49$ modulo $23$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The additive inverse of $-49$ modulo $23$ is the integer $0\\le x<23$ such that\n\n$$\nx+(-49)≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,23).\n$$\n\nFirst, we note that $-49≡20\\,(\\text{mod}\\,23):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-49 & ≡(-3)\\cdot 23+20 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,23) \\\\  & ≡(-3)\\cdot 0+20 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,23) \\\\  & ≡20 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,23)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, note that $-20+20≡0,$ so $x≡-20\\,(\\text{mod}\\,23).$ To write this in the required form, we use the following sequence of congruences:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ≡-20 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,23) \\\\  & ≡0-20 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,23) \\\\  & ≡23-20 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,23) \\\\  & ≡3 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,23)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $-49$ modulo $23$ is $3.$\n\nWe can verify this result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-49+3≡-46≡(-2)\\cdot 23≡0\\,\\,✓\\,(\\text{mod}\\,23)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** In general, the additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a\\,\\text{mod}\\,n.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-09b0eb5f-c65b-5b03-8dcb-9c5edf19b005"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-09b0eb5f-c65b-5b03-8dcb-9c5edf19b005" :answer-field/id #uuid "09b0eb5f-c65b-5b03-8dcb-9c5edf19b005" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e1498b41-ea7b-5297-b0d9-57e9714e3802" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e1498b41-ea7b-5297-b0d9-57e9714e3802"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e1498b41-ea7b-5297-b0d9-57e9714e3802" :answer/id #uuid "e1498b41-ea7b-5297-b0d9-57e9714e3802" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-06e3421b-201f-5b72-a27d-eae8c015169e" :question/id #uuid "06e3421b-201f-5b72-a27d-eae8c015169e" :question/math-academy-id "q-213365" :question/problem "Select the correct options in the reasoning below." :question/worked-solution "The additive inverse of $18$ modulo $48$ is the integer $0\\le x<48$ such that\n\n$$\nx+18≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,48).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that when we add our two numbers, we get a number that is *not* congruent to zero modulo $48:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}34+18 & ≡52 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,48) \\\\  & ≡48+4 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,48) \\\\  & ≡4 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,48) \\\\  & ≢0 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,48)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude the following:\n\nThe integer $34$ $\\text{is not}$ the additive inverse of $18$ modulo $48$ since $34+18≢0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,48).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a78d976f-e2bc-56a5-a4bb-73400d46fa79" "answer-field-cdf84a87-289f-51bb-8740-b94f6824a94e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a78d976f-e2bc-56a5-a4bb-73400d46fa7