d #uuid "60b1fda4-60e8-5732-9f6d-dacad47edd54" :question/math-academy-id "q-213368" :question/problem "Select the correct options in the reasoning below." :question/worked-solution "The additive inverse of $13$ modulo $37$ is the integer $0\\le x<37$ such that\n\n$$\nx+13≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,37).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that when we add our two numbers, we get a number that is *not* congruent to zero modulo $37:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14+13 & ≡27 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,37) \\\\  & ≢0 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,37)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude the following:\n\nThe integer $14$ $\\text{is not}$ the additive inverse of $13$ modulo $27$ since $14+13≢0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,37).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3ac6fe02-2088-51ff-bf85-c0c24991608b" "answer-field-d4aa52c3-dfab-5d6f-bee1-9245f9a77b68"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3ac6fe02-2088-51ff-bf85-c0c24991608b" :answer-field/id #uuid "3ac6fe02-2088-51ff-bf85-c0c24991608b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-4c170b44-ff95-5507-a350-d4e5c2f60a48" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cb79e7c1-683f-59c0-a8d6-df3d0d51f66e" "answer-4c170b44-ff95-5507-a350-d4e5c2f60a48"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb79e7c1-683f-59c0-a8d6-df3d0d51f66e" :answer/id #uuid "cb79e7c1-683f-59c0-a8d6-df3d0d51f66e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "is" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4c170b44-ff95-5507-a350-d4e5c2f60a48" :answer/id #uuid "4c170b44-ff95-5507-a350-d4e5c2f60a48" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "is not" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d4aa52c3-dfab-5d6f-bee1-9245f9a77b68" :answer-field/id #uuid "d4aa52c3-dfab-5d6f-bee1-9245f9a77b68" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-fd795f6e-bdd2-5040-8e42-7f7fd66a4b77" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5c299b33-1ac9-59e6-86b3-a2f7feb6ee95" "answer-9bb38c5f-c774-5eb8-abda-40c90ec1794f" "answer-fd795f6e-bdd2-5040-8e42-7f7fd66a4b77" "answer-fa8f4f92-4440-5453-a44d-27acef6eebf7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c299b33-1ac9-59e6-86b3-a2f7feb6ee95" :answer/id #uuid "5c299b33-1ac9-59e6-86b3-a2f7feb6ee95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "≡0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9bb38c5f-c774-5eb8-abda-40c90ec1794f" :answer/id #uuid "9bb38c5f-c774-5eb8-abda-40c90ec1794f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "≡1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd795f6e-bdd2-5040-8e42-7f7fd66a4b77" :answer/id #uuid "fd795f6e-bdd2-5040-8e42-7f7fd66a4b77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "≢0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa8f4f92-4440-5453-a44d-27acef6eebf7" :answer/id #uuid "fa8f4f92-4440-5453-a44d-27acef6eebf7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "≢1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0c1ec073-8757-564a-9c57-9cebe1d4c92b" :question/id #uuid "0c1ec073-8757-564a-9c57-9cebe1d4c92b" :question/math-academy-id "q-213362" :question/problem "Select the correct options in the reasoning below." :question/worked-solution "The additive inverse of $16$ modulo $25$ is the integer $0\\le x<25$ such that\n\n$$\nx+16≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,25).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that when we add our two numbers, we get a number that is congruent to zero modulo $25:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9+16 & ≡25 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,25) \\\\  & ≡0 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,25)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude the following:\n\nThe integer $9$ $\\text{is}$ the additive inverse of $16$ modulo $25$ since $9+16≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,25).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1fb06d60-5fe7-5fd5-941c-b4e04e76813f" "answer-field-67bfa4fa-c10e-578f-bb8f-5a7b76593ee3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1fb06d60-5fe7-5fd5-941c-b4e04e76813f" :answer-field/id #uuid "1fb06d60-5fe7-5fd5-941c-b4e04e76813f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-6bf4ad5a-a756-52c7-993b-26da07d89c56" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6bf4ad5a-a756-52c7-993b-26da07d89c56" "answer-b09a308c-49a0-56b5-bd3c-02f0365c3548"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6bf4ad5a-a756-52c7-993b-26da07d89c56" :answer/id #uuid "6bf4ad5a-a756-52c7-993b-26da07d89c56" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "is" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b09a308c-49a0-56b5-bd3c-02f0365c3548" :answer/id #uuid "b09a308c-49a0-56b5-bd3c-02f0365c3548" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "is not" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-67bfa4fa-c10e-578f-bb8f-5a7b76593ee3" :answer-field/id #uuid "67bfa4fa-c10e-578f-bb8f-5a7b76593ee3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-06ae9272-d8f2-5789-9c55-fc770364606e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-06ae9272-d8f2-5789-9c55-fc770364606e" "answer-7f52f8c1-53ad-583d-97d1-f7dc928796f5" "answer-71da0f9a-829f-556c-aaa6-adb577aa666c" "answer-36efb386-b485-5d7e-8f43-e1f6d9f72ce4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06ae9272-d8f2-5789-9c55-fc770364606e" :answer/id #uuid "06ae9272-d8f2-5789-9c55-fc770364606e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "≡0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7f52f8c1-53ad-583d-97d1-f7dc928796f5" :answer/id #uuid "7f52f8c1-53ad-583d-97d1-f7dc928796f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "≡1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-71da0f9a-829f-556c-aaa6-adb577aa666c" :answer/id #uuid "71da0f9a-829f-556c-aaa6-adb577aa666c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "≢0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-36efb386-b485-5d7e-8f43-e1f6d9f72ce4" :answer/id #uuid "36efb386-b485-5d7e-8f43-e1f6d9f72ce4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "≢1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186153470 :tutorial/content "The **additive inverse** of $a$ modulo $n$ is the integer $0 \\leq x \\lt n$ such that\n\n$$\nx + a \\equiv 0 \\quad (\\textrm{mod} \\: n).\n$$\n\nFor example, the integer $7$ is the additive inverse of $5$ modulo $12$ since \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7+5≡12≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,12).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe can visualize this using a clock diagram.\n\n![](images/5f/5f0c578480e9f9f80820108a0af79ae8eecc826127c6e4d44aa5f3b50a6f086a.png)\n\nOn the other hand, the integer $6$ is *not* the additive inverse of $5$ modulo $12$ since $6 + 5 \\equiv 11\\not\\equiv 0 \\, (\\textrm{mod} \\: 12).$ \n\nIn general, we have the following theorem:\n\n*For every integer, there exists a unique additive inverse for a given modulus $n.$* \n\nNote the following: \n\n- The word \"unique\" in the statement above means with respect to the inequality $0 \\leq x \\lt n.$\n\n- It's important to know that any integer summed with an integer congruent to its inverse will also give zero. \n\nFor example, $x=7$ is the additive inverse of $5$ modulo $12.$ But since $19\\equiv 7\\:(\\textrm{mod}\\: 12),$ we have that the sum of $5$ and $19$ is also congruent to $0{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}19+5≡24≡2\\cdot 12≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,12)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's see some more examples." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152355 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
